2] Dependency Injection (DI)

Q] What is dependency Injection.
- It is design Pattern.
- As Java application is build using multiple classes and Dependency. i.e One class is depend on other class.
  For example
  Class A {
            public void Work{}
          }
   Class B {
            A obj;
            public void DoWork{}
            }

Class B is depend on Class A, in Legecy System We are manaually creating this object and passing it,
Now dependency Injection Will handle it.


Q] What is IOC container

Ans :-  IOC container responsible for creating objects, holding them in memory and injecting them if necessary,
        It will maintain the lifecycle of objects.
        It is predefined program, 

        We need to Provide two Things to IOC container
        1] Beans Or Classes
        2] Configuration - We need to Mention which Bean is dependent on another bean.


Q] Who Represents IOC Container

- ApplicationContext Interface Represents IOC container.
- ApplicationContext Extends BeanFactory. It has Additional Things from BeanFactory.
- Three classes Extends Application Context Interface
   - ClassPathXmlApplicationContext
   - AnnotationConfigApplicationContext
   - FileSystemXmlApplicationContext



Q] What are the ways to do Dependency Injection

1] Constructor Injection.
