Stereotype Annotation

@Component :- this is class level annotation, It will tell spring we need to create object of this class
           :- It will follow CamaleCase Object creation i.e If class Name Is Anand it will create object as anand
              we can give implicit name at time of declaration @Component("ak") object will represent as ak now

@Value :-we can add Values to Variables implicitly using @Value Annotation.


@Scope :- Used to define the scope of bean, i.e how many instances of bean should be created and how long they should alive.
Types :- * singleton(default) :  only one instance per SpringContainer
         * prototype : A new Instance Everytime bean is required
         * request : One instance per HTTP request ( Only for webapps )

@Configuration :- It tells Spring that the class can be used by the Spring IoC container as a source of bean definitions.

@ComponentScan(base Package = ):-


@Bean :-  is a Spring annotation used inside a class annotated with @Configuration.
It tells Spring that the method will return an object that should be registered as a Spring Bean in the application context.


